# Line endings: LF on every OS, so a Windows checkout reads the same bytes as Linux's. (An idea's hash
# normalizes CRLF, but the programs' text, the goldens and the scripts must not change with the OS.)
* text=auto eol=lf
# The bench's reports are kept as the bench wrote them, byte for byte: a Windows runner's report
# quotes its compilers' messages with their CRLF line endings.
docs/benchmarks/BENCHMARKS-*.md -text
